   "subject": "Rangefinder for distance sampling in tropical forest",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi<div>I&#39;m planning a distance sampling survey for a tropical forest bird species (Príncipe Thrush - <i>Turdus xanthorhynchus</i>) and am wondering what type of rangefinder to use . Distances likely to be in the region of 5-30 meters. Does anyone have a preferred rangefinder model? Would a basic golf/hunting model like this be suitable <a href=\"https://www.amazon.co.uk/TACKLIFE-Continuous-Magnification-Measurement-Waterproof/dp/B07H3JS5L1/ref=sr_1_5?keywords=rangefinder&amp;qid=1556790370&amp;s=gateway&amp;sr=8-5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.amazon.co.uk/TACKLIFE-Continuous-Magnification-Measurement-Waterproof/dp/B07H3JS5L1/ref%3Dsr_1_5?keywords%3Drangefinder%26qid%3D1556790370%26s%3Dgateway%26sr%3D8-5&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474071076000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1QL__m5onTiNOVKLpZNKLI\">www.amazon.co.uk/TACKLIFE</a>?</div><div>Cheers</div><div>Frazer</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "atSPI5rDAwAJ",
